The pass told the agent to send revisions with -v N but said nothing
about an interdiff, so revised series went out without one and the
reviewer had to reread every patch to find what changed. It now names
the previous version with --previous, which format-patch.sh needs to
rebuild that version from the list, and says what to do when the
revision moved to a new base. The mail workflow guide states the same
rule.
