-**Revisions.** For a revised series add `-v N`. Address every review
-point the list researcher found unaddressed, or say why not. End the
-cover letter blurb with what changed and a link to the previous
-version:
+**Revisions.** For a revised series add `-v N` and
+`--previous=<message-id of the v(N-1) cover>`, or of its only patch.
+format-patch.sh refuses a reroll without it. It rebuilds v(N-1) from
+the list onto `--base` with series-rebuild.sh and adds an interdiff
+against it, so the reviewer sees exactly what changed since the
+version they read, computed from that mail rather than from your
+tree. If v(N-1) does not apply onto the new base, it says so and adds
+a range-diff instead; say in the cover letter why the base moved.
+
+Address every review point the list researcher found unaddressed, or
+say why not. End the cover letter blurb with what changed and a link
+to the previous version:
 
     Changes in vN:
     - <what changed, and why>
